    endpoint('/nat-audit/events','get','All retained NAT events, newest receipt first',R('NatEventPage'),[param('deviceId',S(maxLength=64),True),param('from',T),param('to',T),param('protocol',I(minimum=0,maximum=255)),param('privateIp',S(maxLength=45)),param('publicIp',S(maxLength=45)),param('limit',I(minimum=1,maximum=100,default=50)),param('cursor',S(maxLength=800))],description='Default all retained history: omit BOTH from and to. An explicit range requires both bounds with from < to; no fixed day cap. The first request freezes its upper cutoff, returned cursors bind organization/device/filters/range and paginate by (receivedAt,id) descending. A receipt-ordered lightweight index examines at most 128 candidates, then canonical FINAL identity lookup rejects later replays. A page can be empty while nextCursor remains non-null when candidates were replays; continue until the cursor is null. Each query has 128 MiB read/memory, two threads and four second server budgets; sparse filters that exceed them return 503, never a false empty success. UDP observations retain COMPLETENESS_NOT_GUARANTEED; no full session reconstruction is implied.')
    endpoint('/devices/{id}/bandwidth/heatmap','get','Seven local dates of device aggregate bandwidth with an optional square matrix',R('Heatmap'),[param('timezone',S(),True),param('direction',S(enum=['rx','tx'],default='rx')),param('days',I(enum=[7],default=7)),param('statistic',S(enum=['sample_mean','time_weighted_mean'],default='time_weighted_mean')),param('gridSize',I(enum=[0,7,28],default=0))],description="Owned device's named rx/tx bandwidth gauge, aggregated from all original stored observations into 168 local-hour cells. Optional gridSize 7 or 28 additionally returns 49 or 784 distinct chronological matrix intervals spanning the same seven local dates through the next local midnight. Five-minute ticks are distributed over those intervals; each carries its actual UTC bounds, including DST. Means and sample counts are computed directly from valid original observations within each interval, never by averaging hourly means or copying/interpolating coarse cells. Raw reads are bounded at 100000 samples and 2 MiB; exceeding a bound fails explicitly. Both views share the same read; query limits and admission budgets are unchanged. No interface re-summing occurs. Response interfaceId is __device__, statistic is sample_mean and coverage estimates observed-sample count against the inferred sampling cadence, not counter-delta duration coverage. Device aggregate includes the collector's observed interfaces; logical and physical interfaces can overlap, disclosed by INTERFACE_OVERLAP_POSSIBLE. Null remains unavailable. Original per-interface counter-rollup endpoint remains available.")
